  "reading": "xFV still predicts WAR; the blend lambda is HOW MUCH to trust xFV's adjustment over the consensus anchor. WAG (realized over/underperformance vs consensus FV = where consensus MISSED) sets lambda WHEN its predicted-edge -> realized-WAG regression has signal (hitters, spearman ~0.20). When that regression is non-significant (pitchers, spearman ~0.02) WAG's slope is noise -- it pinned pitchers at 0.391, which the eval shows DRAGGING the ridge (rho 0.281) back toward consensus (blend 0.2625). There lambda is sized by the rank gate directly (rank_calibration): pooled+within-tier+FV45-fringe maximized in a conservative [0.50,0.70] band -> ~0.65, lifting pooled OOS rho to ~0.28 (the robust, CI-positive part of the available gain)."
